                    "content": "## Standard Discrete Distributions\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Distribution | PMF \\(P(X=x)\\) | Mean | Variance | MGF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Bernoulli\\((p)\\) | \\(p^x q^{1-x}\\), \\(x=0,1\\) | \\(p\\) | \\(pq\\) | \\(q+pe^t\\) |\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\(\\binom{n}{x}p^x q^{n-x}\\) | \\(np\\) | \\(npq\\) | \\((q+pe^t)^n\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(e^{-\\lambda}\\lambda^x/x!\\) | \\(\\lambda\\) | \\(\\lambda\\) | \\(e^{\\lambda(e^t-1)}\\) |\n| Geometric\\((p)\\) | \\(q^x p\\), \\(x=0,1,2,\\ldots\\) | \\(q/p\\) | \\(q/p^2\\) | \\(p(1-qe^t)^{-1}\\) |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | \\(\\binom{x+r-1}{x}p^r q^x\\) | \\(rq/p\\) | \\(rq/p^2\\) | \\((p/(1-qe^t))^r\\) |\n| Hypergeometric | \\(\\frac{\\binom{M}{x}\\binom{N-M}{n-x}}{\\binom{N}{n}}\\) | \\(nM/N\\) | \\(n\\frac{M}{N}\\frac{N-M}{N}\\frac{N-n}{N-1}\\) | — |\n| Multinomial | \\(\\frac{n!}{x_1!\\cdots x_k!}p_1^{x_1}\\cdots p_k^{x_k}\\) | \\(np_i\\) | \\(np_i q_i\\) | \\((\\sum p_i e^{t_i})^n\\) |\n\n### Skewness & Kurtosis\n\n| Distribution | \\(\\gamma_1\\) (Skewness) | \\(\\beta_2\\) (Kurtosis) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\(\\frac{q-p}{\\sqrt{npq}}\\) | \\(3 + \\frac{1-6pq}{npq}\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(1/\\sqrt{\\lambda}\\) | \\(3 + 1/\\lambda\\) |\n| Geometric\\((p)\\) | \\(\\frac{2-p}{\\sqrt{q}}\\) | \\(3 + \\frac{p^2+6q}{q}\\) |\n\n### PGFs\n\n| Distribution | PGF \\(G(s) = E(s^X)\\) |\n|---|---|\n| Bernoulli\\((p)\\) | \\(q + ps\\) |\n| Binomial\\((n,p)\\) | \\((q+ps)^n\\) |\n| Poisson\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(e^{\\lambda(s-1)}\\) |\n| Geometric\\((p)\\) | \\(p/(1-qs)\\) |\n| NegBin\\((r,p)\\) | \\((p/(1-qs))^r\\) |\n\n### Key Properties & Relationships\n\n- **Poisson as limit of Binomial:** \\(B(n,p) \\to \\text{Poisson}(\\lambda)\\) as \\(n \\to \\infty\\), \\(p \\to 0\\), \\(np \\to \\lambda\\)\n- **Poisson cumulants:** ALL cumulants = \\(\\lambda\\) — unique property\n- **Geometric memoryless:** \\(P(X > m+n | X > m) = P(X > n)\\)\n- **NegBin = sum of \\(r\\) independent Geometric RVs**\n- **Hypergeometric → Binomial** when \\(N \\to \\infty\\), \\(M/N \\to p\\)\n- **Multinomial marginals** are Binomial: \\(X_i \\sim B(n, p_i)\\)\n- **Finite population correction** in Hypergeometric: \\((N-n)/(N-1)\\)\n\n> **ISS tip:** Poisson has mean = variance = \\(\\lambda\\). Geometric is the only discrete memoryless distribution. Hypergeometric variance has the FPC factor \\((N-n)/(N-1)\\). Binomial → Poisson approximation conditions: \\(n\\) large, \\(p\\) small, \\(np\\) moderate."
