                    "content": "## Standard Continuous Distributions\n\n### Core Distributions Table\n\n| Distribution | PDF | Mean | Variance | Skewness \\(\\gamma_1\\) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Uniform\\((a,b)\\) | \\(1/(b-a)\\) | \\((a+b)/2\\) | \\((b-a)^2/12\\) | \\(0\\) |\n| Exponential\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\(\\lambda e^{-\\lambda x}\\) | \\(1/\\lambda\\) | \\(1/\\lambda^2\\) | \\(2\\) |\n| Normal\\((\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\) | \\(\\frac{1}{\\sigma\\sqrt{2\\pi}}e^{-(x-\\mu)^2/2\\sigma^2}\\) | \\(\\mu\\) | \\(\\sigma^2\\) | \\(0\\) |\n| Cauchy\\((\\mu,1)\\) | \\(\\frac{1}{\\pi(1+(x-\\mu)^2)}\\) | undefined | undefined | undefined |\n| Laplace\\((\\mu,b)\\) | \\(\\frac{1}{2b}e^{-|x-\\mu|/b}\\) | \\(\\mu\\) | \\(2b^2\\) | \\(0\\) |\n| Gamma\\((\\alpha,\\lambda)\\) | \\(\\frac{\\lambda^\\alpha}{\\Gamma(\\alpha)}x^{\\alpha-1}e^{-\\lambda x}\\) | \\(\\alpha/\\lambda\\) | \\(\\alpha/\\lambda^2\\) | \\(2/\\sqrt{\\alpha}\\) |\n| Beta\\((m,n)\\) | \\(\\frac{x^{m-1}(1-x)^{n-1}}{B(m,n)}\\) | \\(m/(m+n)\\) | \\(\\frac{mn}{(m+n)^2(m+n+1)}\\) | — |\n| Lognormal\\((\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\) | — | \\(e^{\\mu+\\sigma^2/2}\\) | \\((e^{\\sigma^2}-1)e^{2\\mu+\\sigma^2}\\) | — |\n\n### MGFs\n\n| Distribution | MGF \\(M_X(t)\\) |\n|---|---|\n| Uniform\\((a,b)\\) | \\(\\frac{e^{tb}-e^{ta}}{t(b-a)}\\) |\n| Exponential\\((\\lambda)\\) | \\((1-t/\\lambda)^{-1}\\), \\(t<\\lambda\\) |\n| Normal\\((\\mu,\\sigma^2)\\) | \\(e^{\\mu t + \\sigma^2 t^2/2}\\) |\n| Cauchy | Does NOT exist |\n| Laplace\\((\\mu,b)\\) | \\(e^{\\mu t}/(1-b^2t^2)\\), \\(|t|<1/b\\) |\n| Gamma\\((\\alpha,\\lambda)\\) | \\((1-t/\\lambda)^{-\\alpha}\\), \\(t<\\lambda\\) |\n\n### Special Properties\n\n- **Normal:** Only distribution with \\(\\kappa_r = 0\\) for \\(r \\ge 3\\); symmetric; \\(\\beta_2 = 3\\)\n- **Exponential:** Unique **continuous memoryless** distribution: \\(P(X>s+t|X>s) = P(X>t)\\)\n- **Cauchy:** Stable distribution; mean/variance undefined; median = \\(\\mu\\); mode = \\(\\mu\\)\n- **Gamma special cases:** \\(\\text{Gamma}(1,\\lambda) = \\text{Exp}(\\lambda)\\); \\(\\text{Gamma}(n/2, 1/2) = \\chi^2(n)\\)\n- **Beta\\((1,1)\\) = Uniform\\((0,1)\\)**\n- **Lognormal:** Median = \\(e^\\mu\\); Mode = \\(e^{\\mu-\\sigma^2}\\); positively skewed\n- **Laplace:** Double exponential; \\(\\beta_2 = 6\\) (leptokurtic)\n\n---\n\n### Bivariate Normal Distribution\n\n**PDF:**\n\\[\nf(x,y) = \\frac{1}{2\\pi\\sigma_1\\sigma_2\\sqrt{1-\\rho^2}} \\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{1}{2(1-\\rho^2)}\\left[\\frac{(x-\\mu_1)^2}{\\sigma_1^2} - \\frac{2\\rho(x-\\mu_1)(y-\\mu_2)}{\\sigma_1\\sigma_2} + \\frac{(y-\\mu_2)^2}{\\sigma_2^2}\\right]\\right)\n\\]\n\n**Parameters:** \\((\\mu_1, \\mu_2, \\sigma_1^2, \\sigma_2^2, \\rho)\\)\n\n**Marginals:** \\(X \\sim N(\\mu_1,\\sigma_1^2)\\), \\(Y \\sim N(\\mu_2,\\sigma_2^2)\\)\n\n**Conditional distribution of \\(X\\) given \\(Y=y\\):**\n\\[\nX|Y=y \\;\\sim\\; N\\!\\left(\\mu_1 + \\rho\\frac{\\sigma_1}{\\sigma_2}(y-\\mu_2),\\; \\sigma_1^2(1-\\rho^2)\\right)\n\\]\n\n**Key property:** For Bivariate Normal, \\(\\rho = 0 \\iff X \\perp Y\\) (unique to normal!)\n\n**Linear combinations:** \\(aX + bY \\sim N(a\\mu_1+b\\mu_2,\\; a^2\\sigma_1^2 + 2ab\\rho\\sigma_1\\sigma_2 + b^2\\sigma_2^2)\\)\n\n> **ISS tip:** Exponential is the ONLY continuous memoryless distribution. Cauchy has no MGF and no moments. Bivariate Normal: \\(\\rho=0\\) implies independence (unlike general case). Lognormal mean \\(\\ne e^\\mu\\) — it's \\(e^{\\mu+\\sigma^2/2}\\)."
