            "tips": "**ISS Paper I — Probability & Statistical Methods priorities:**\n- **Convergence hierarchy:** a.s. ⟹ in probability ⟹ in distribution; m.s. ⟹ in probability\n- **Zero-one laws:** Borel–Cantelli Part 2 requires independence + divergent series\n- **Chebyshev:** \\(P(|X-\\mu|\\ge k\\sigma) \\le 1/k^2\\) — no assumption on distribution\n- **CLT:** requires finite variance; proved using continuity theorem + CFs\n- **Bivariate Normal:** \\(\\rho=0 \\Leftrightarrow\\) independence (unique to BVN)\n- **Jacobian:** for transformations — draw the region, check one-to-one\n- **\\(t_n^2 = F_{1,n}\\)** and **\\(F_{m,n} = 1/F_{n,m}\\)** — exam favourites\n- **ARE:** Sign = \\(2/\\pi \\approx 0.637\\), Wilcoxon = \\(3/\\pi \\approx 0.955\\) vs t-test for Normal\n- **Order statistics:** \\(E(X_{(r)}) = r/(n+1)\\) for Uniform; learn the PDF formula\n- **Multiple R ∈ [0,1]; Partial r ∈ [-1,1]** — do not confuse bounds"
